-- title:
--   prog as IL procedures (bit data)
-- statement:
--   **`prog` as IL procedures (bit data).** For a fixed circuit over `ZMod 2` whose frame changes have `0/1` permutation parts and whose Lemma 10 shifts have coefficients `±k'·d⁻¹` (`k', d ≤ D`) at every field size `q ^ m ^ j`, the procedure table `progTbl` (one procedure per reachable configuration; level `j + 1` procedures call level `j` ones) runs the root procedure from the encoded input to the encoded `prog C q k P L A B Cs xs`, with cost `ilCost C D q Bb k V (|A| + |B| + |Cs|)`.
